"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_smlm_controls.py, for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_smlm_controls --tests tests/test_exp_smlm_controls.py --raw results/smlm/controls_raw.npz --md results/smlm/controls.md --out-env CONTROLS_OUT \\
        --spec tools/mutants/wp_smlmcontrols_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence in experiments/exp_smlm_controls.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone (`pytest -x`; the two tests that
read the stored raw run on the copy of it in the slot; everything else is planted). Ids: K the constants, P the path statistics, O the forced order, S the scoring helpers, V the validation runs, G the
greedy part on planted frames, A the offset-corrected objective and its ascent, Q the search and the Picasso part (a stub worker), D the detections of a method, E the set evaluation, T the report,
U the gap statistics, M the command line.

Result on the 36 tests of tests/test_exp_smlm_controls.py (the unmutated source passes the control with them and regenerates the md unchanged): 228 mutants, 226 killed, 2 survivors that change no output
(equivalent mutants, left in on purpose):
  Q31  `objective='plain'` for `'offset-corrected'` in the signature that guards the resumable search cache of `part_ps`: the string only matters across two versions of the script that share a cache
       directory; within one version both spellings give the same signature and the same results;
  Q32  `gt['frame'] >= d0` without the upper bound for the development ground truth in `part_ps`: every score is taken on the frames `dev_idx` (`smlm_common.score` looks up the ground truth of those frames
       only), so ground truth of later frames is never read.
Order of work: a first complete pass left 41 survivors (the md column showed which of them changed the report); the killable ones got an assertion or a test (constants of the border and the digest, the offset
being that of the pairing of all emitters, the counted calls of the filter cache, the half-point improvement of the ascent, the first line search, the guard check on at most 20 frames, the frames that
differ, the means and extremes over two sets, the gap intervals, the NaN resamples, the dense-set columns), the 41 were run again (39 killed; D09 needed a direct assertion on the J point's detections and
was killed by a third run), and the 2 above remain.

Not mutated, on purpose: `part_ref`, `part_g13`, `part_gb16`, `part_gb13` and `pic_setup` read the frozen raws and the SMLM data, which the tests do not have; they were exercised by the real run
(the stored rows they wrote are checked by the two raw-reading tests: the development score of each stored operating point equals the one recorded by the frozen selection, the search records equal the
stored corrected detections' scores) and `part_meta` records digests. `main`'s `--run` branch loops over these parts.
"""
